THE CODE / CONTENT BOUNDARY
===========================

Two licences apply to this repository, and they cover disjoint sets of files.

  LICENSE          GNU AGPL-3.0-or-later. Covers the Program: all source code,
                   configuration, build scripts, tests and styles.

  LICENSE-CONTENT  All rights reserved. Covers the SITE CONTENT: everything
                   under `src/content/`, the wireframes under `docs/wireframe*/`,
                   the PZGIF name and brand assets, and all explanatory prose,
                   FAQ text and marketing copy.

The SITE CONTENT is a separate work. It is not part of the Program, it is not
required to run or modify the Program, and it is not conveyed under the AGPL.
Site content is kept in `.md` / `.mdx` / `.json` data files rather than in `.tsx`
modules precisely so this boundary is visible in the file tree.

`messages/` is **Program**, not SITE CONTENT. Those are interface strings the
Program cannot run without, so withholding them would break the AGPL's
Corresponding Source requirement. Marketing and explainer prose belongs in
`src/content/`.


SOURCE OFFER (AGPL-3.0 §6)
==========================

AGPL-3.0 §6 requires the Corresponding Source for the version conveyed, not for
whatever happens to be on the default branch. The footer "Source" link on every
page therefore resolves to the exact commit the running bundle was built from,
and `scripts/check-source-sha.mjs` fetches that commit anonymously from the
public repository URL — no credentials, no local refs — so a commit that is
unpushed, or a repository that is private, fails CI on `main`. Once a host is
chosen it must be wired ahead of the deploy step.


PERMANENCE
==========

The PZGIF frontend is AGPL permanently. A future Pro or API tier will share this
tool registry, design system, components and copy, all AGPL by then. Monetisation
comes from the hosted service and the API, not from code secrecy. Any closed
component must be server-only and must invoke unmodified gifski out-of-process.
See docs/tech-stack.md for the full rationale and the exit that was rejected.


